Since we are in the middle of migrating from discordeno 17 to 21, here are some tips (Taken from the Discordeno Discord Server https://discord.com/channels/785384884197392384/1307773501532536903/1307786395682738228):

This guide only covers a part of the changes and not all (yet). Please use TS if you don't, otherwise you will cry.

## Bot

`JsonErrorCodes`, `Errors` exports are removed

###  createBot:

### Options: 
First and foremost: You should set up desired properties

`botId` -> `applicationId`
`secretKey` -> moved to `proxy.authorization` in `rest` property

### Methods / Properties:

`bot.helpers.getAvatarURL`, `bot.helpers.getGuildIconURL` -> import `avatarUrl`, `guildIconUrl`
`bot.helpers.xxx` -> either in `rest.xxx` or `gateway.xxx`, but most also being aliased in `bot.helpers.xxx` for backwards compatibility, `bot.helpers.xxx` will go through transformers etc. and only give you the desired properties, `rest.xxx` for example will give you all props Discord returns

`options` param in `bot.helpers.sendFollowupMessage` now accepts `InteractionCallbackData` instead of `InteractionResponse`

Helpers that fetches from api and returns collections will now return array instead (For example `bot.helpers.getReactions`)

`embeds` in `bot.helpers.sendMessage` is now `DiscordEmbed[]` instead of `Embed[]`, `file` is now `files` as `FileContent[]`

`reason` prop in `options` param of `bot.helpers.createInvite`, `bot.helpers.editChannel` etc. have been moved to a third param instead

`bot.utils.xxx` is moved to their respective places. For example, `bot.utils.calculateShardId` is now at `gateway.calculateShardId`, some functions like `bot.utils.delay` are now a global export
`bot.constants.routes` is moved to `rest.routes` and has been reworked

`Role.botId`, `Role.integrationId` -> `Role.tags.botId`, `Role.tags.integrationId`

`Message.authorId`, `Message.isFromBot` -> `Message.author.id`, `Message.author.bot`
`Message.flags` has change from `number` to `ToggleBitfield`


### Handlers:

The types is changed from
`(bot: Bot, data: DiscordGatewayPayload, shardId: number)` to
`(bot: typeof bot, data: DiscordGatewayPayload, shardId: number)`

### Events:

First parameter (bot) is removed

### Transformers:

`transformers.reverse.interactionResponse` is removed

## Gateway:

`createShardManager` is removed

### createGatewayManager:

### Options:

`gatewayBot` -> `connection`
`gatewayConfig.xxx` -> `xxx`
`handleDiscordPayload` is removed
`tellWorkerToIdentify` is removed from options, you can use it from `manager` (return type of `createGatewayManager()`)

### Methods / Properties:
`gateway.manager` - `gateway` itself is now GatewayManager
`gateway.calculateShardId` - first parameter (gateway) is removed

`manager.createShardOptions.makePresence` -> `manager.makePresence`, `activities[number].createdAt` -> `since`
`manager.createShardOptions.events`, `manager.createShardOptions.identify` -> `manager.events`, `manager.identify`
`manager.createShardOptions.send` -> `manager.sendPayload` (but `highPriority` param is not there, you can use `shard.send` if you need it)

## Rest:

### createRestManager:

### Options: 
`secretKey` -> `proxy.authorization`
`customUrl` -> `proxy.baseUrl`

### Methods / Properties:

`runMethod` -> `makeRequest`, first param (rest) is removed